[[:db/cas 17592186311877 :question/problem "Consider the following differential operator:\n\n$$\nD(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}\n$$\n\nFill in the steps in the reasoning below.\n\nFor any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={{field-2}}+{{field-3}} \\\\  & +2ab\\cdot {{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+b{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since {{field-5}} \nthe operator $D$ is {{field-6}}." "Consider the following differential operator:\n\n$$\nD(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}\n$$\n\nFill in the steps in the reasoning below.\n\nFor any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n<div class=\"question-equation\">\n<div>$D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=$ {{field-2}} $+$ {{field-3}}</div>\n<div>$ {}+2ab\\cdot$ {{field-4}}.</div>\n</div>\n\nWe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}+b{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}\\right)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since {{field-5}} \nthe operator $D$ is {{field-6}}."] [:db/cas 17592186311880 :question/problem "Consider the following differential operator:\n\n$