}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={{field-2}}-2\\cdot {{field-3}} \\\\  & +ab\\cdot {{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a\\left[{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{1}\\right]+b\\left[{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{2}\\right] \\\\  & =a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since {{field-5}} \nthe operator $D$ is {{field-6}}." "Consider the following differential operator:\n\n$$\nD(y)=y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y\n$$\n\nFill in the steps in the reasoning below.\n\nFor any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\n$$\n\n<div class=\"question-equation\">\n<div>$D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=$ {{field-2}} $-2\\cdot$ {{field-3}}</div>\n<div>$ {}+ab\\cdot$ {{field-4}}.</div>\n</div>\n\nWe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a\\left[{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{1}\\right]+b\\left[{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{2}\\right] \\\\  & =a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since {{field-5}} \nthe operator $D$ is {{field-6}}."] [:db/ensure 17592186311877 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186311880 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186311915 :question/validate]]
